## Summary

Implement a knowledge graph that builds relationship graphs between context items, enabling relationship extraction, graph traversal, and persistence for understanding how context items relate to each other.

## Motivation

Without knowledge graph:
- No visibility into relationships between context items
- Cannot find related concepts efficiently
- No structured knowledge representation
- Limited reasoning about context dependencies

Knowledge graph enables structured knowledge navigation.

## Technical Approach

### Goals
- Define `KnowledgeGraph` struct with nodes and edges
- Implement relationship extraction from context
- Support graph traversal API (`get_related`)
- Persist graph for reuse

### Implementation Details

```rust
// crates/astra-context-intel/src/knowledge_graph.rs

/// Knowledge graph node
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct KnowledgeNode {
    pub id: String,
    pub context_item_id: String,
    pub node_type: NodeType,
    pub label: String,
    pub properties: HashMap<String, String>,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub enum NodeType {
    Concept,
    Entity,
    Fact,
    Decision,
    Requirement,
}

/// Knowledge graph edge
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct KnowledgeEdge {
    pub id: String,
    pub from_node: String,
    pub to_node: String,
    pub relation_type: RelationType,
    pub weight: f32,
    pub properties: HashMap<String, String>,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub enum RelationType {
    RelatedTo,
    DependsOn,
    Contradicts,
    Supports,
    DerivedFrom,
    PartOf,
    Implements,
}

/// Knowledge graph builder
pub struct KnowledgeGraphBuilder {
    model_gateway: Arc<ModelGateway>,
    embedding_model: Arc<dyn EmbeddingModel>,
    similarity_threshold: f32,
}

impl KnowledgeGraphBuilder {
    /// Build graph from context items
    pub async fn build(
        &self,
        items: Vec<ContextItem>,
    ) -> Result<KnowledgeGraph, AstraError> {
        let mut nodes = Vec::new();
        let mut edges = Vec::new();

        // Create nodes from items
        for item in &items {
            let node = self.extract_node(item).await?;
            nodes.push(node);
        }

        // Create edges based on relationships
        for i in 0..nodes.len() {
            for j in (i + 1)..nodes.len() {
                if let Some(edge) = self.detect_relationship(&nodes[i], &nodes[j], &items[i], &items[j]).await? {
                    edges.push(edge);
                }
            }
        }

        Ok(KnowledgeGraph { nodes, edges })
    }

    /// Get related nodes via traversal
    pub fn get_related(
        &self,
        graph: &KnowledgeGraph,
        node_id: &str,
        max_depth: usize,
        max_items: usize,
    ) -> Vec<(KnowledgeNode, Vec<RelationType>, usize)> {
        // BFS traversal
        let mut visited = HashSet::new();
        let mut queue = VecDeque::new();
        let mut results = Vec::new();

        queue.push_back((node_id.to_string(), Vec::new(), 0));

        while let Some((current_id, path, depth)) = queue.pop_front() {
            if depth > max_depth || visited.contains(&current_id) {
                continue;
            }
            visited.insert(current_id.clone());

            if let Some(node) = graph.nodes.iter().find(|n| n.id == current_id) {
                if !path.is_empty() {
                    results.push((node.clone(), path.clone(), depth));
                }

                // Find connected edges
                for edge in &graph.edges {
                    let (next_id, relation) = if edge.from_node == current_id {
                        (&edge.to_node, edge.relation_type.clone())
                    } else if edge.to_node == current_id {
                        (&edge.from_node, edge.relation_type.clone())
                    } else {
                        continue;
                    };

                    let mut new_path = path.clone();
                    new_path.push(relation);
                    queue.push_back((next_id.clone(), new_path, depth + 1));
                }
            }

            if results.len() >= max_items {
                break;
            }
        }

        results
    }
}
```

